---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Changelog | Awesome Coding Plans" description="Notable changes to the Awesome Coding Plans catalog: new plans, price corrections, and site features.">
  <section class="changelog reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">changelog</p>
    <h1>What <span>changed.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Notable catalog and site changes, newest first. Plan bodies carry their own per-plan verified date.</p>

    <section class="entry">
      <h2>October 23, 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Merged vendor correction for Standard Compute (PR #1): explicit $19/mo price, Credits quota model, retired smart pacing, Pro Plus $549/mo budget, refreshed model lineup.</li>
        <li>Cursor restructured pricing: Hobby free, Plus $8, Premium $30 (4x), Super $100 (15x), Ultra $200 (50x); weekly pooled allowance, third-party models at API list price.</li>
        <li>Synthetic now has 3 tiers (Go $9 / Standard $30 / Big $90) with weekly regenerating credits, Fast mode, and Infinite mode beta.</li>
        <li>MiniMax Token Plan closed to new purchases (existing subs keep benefits); new M Plan (Go/Explore/Build) with M3.1 Flash + H3 video documented.</li>
        <li>Trae Lite $8 removed from live pricing page; Kimi tiers renamed with 5h-only window for new members; Qwen added Essential $10 tier + Team Edition.</li>
        <li>MiMo V2.5 retired (V2.6 only); Cline removed 4 deprecated models; OpenCode Go DeepSeek caps corrected; Windsurf SWE-1.7 → SWE-2.</li>
        <li>Google student offer reframed as AI Plus free 1 year; Chutes/NVIDIA/Ollama/Antigravity/Fireworks model and quota corrections.</li>
        <li>Qoder verified via rendered-page fetch: new Lite $10/mo tier (1,000 credits), first-purchase/renewal bonuses, QoderWake Cloud Computer $10/unit.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="entry">
      <h2>October 12, 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Full price re-verification pass across all 33 plans.</li>
        <li>Trae restructured pricing: Lite $8, Pro $20, Pro+ $60, Ultra $200 (SOLO mode on all paid tiers).</li>
        <li>Chutes Base ($3) discontinued — Plus $10 / Pro $20 only; OpenCode Go added Go Plus $40 tier with per-model caps.</li>
        <li>Standard Compute tiers renamed (Starter $19 / Economy $39 / Standard $89 / Pro $249 / Pro Plus $499) with monthly compute budgets.</li>
        <li>Claude models updated to Opus/Sonnet/Haiku 5.5 + Max API credits; OpenAI Codex Pro now $100/$200/$500 tiers with GPT-6 models.</li>
        <li>Windsurf noted as Devin Desktop rebrand with corrected Teams/Enterprise pricing; Qwen moved to monthly credits; MiMo V2.5 deprecation (Oct 21) noted.</li>
        <li>GitHub Copilot student sign-ups reopened; Fireworks Fire Pass marked closed to new subscriptions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="entry">
      <h2>September 4, 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Added Gemini Code Assist, Amazon Q Developer, and Replit Agent plans (catalog now {33} plans).</li>
        <li>Completed machine-readable metadata for every plan: website, models, quota, best-for, and per-plan verified dates in <a href="/plans.json">plans.json</a>.</li>
        <li>Comparison tables now generate from catalog data instead of hand-maintained rows.</li>
        <li>Added browse pages (price, model access, tag, tool), a decision guide, self-hosted fonts, richer SEO metadata, and a custom 404, FAQ, footer, and sitemap covering all plan routes.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="entry">
      <h2>September 3, 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Website launched on Netlify with a filterable catalog, comparison page, and student discounts page.</li>
        <li>Full price verification pass across all listed plans; Fireworks Fire Pass marked discontinued.</li>
        <li>Catalog grew from 19 to 30 plans, including Factory Droid, Augment Code, Qoder Pro, Kilo Code, Trae Pro, and Google Antigravity.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .changelog { max-width: 760px; padding: 4rem 0 2rem; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent); font: 500 .72rem "DM Mono", monospace; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem); line-height: .95; letter-spacing: -.07em; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  h1 span { color: var(--accent); }
  .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .entry { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 1.5rem 0; }
  .entry h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
  .entry ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .entry li { margin: .3rem 0; }
</style>
